      "mergeID": "5bbfd3e934d04545e8ec7c08",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Add enabling/disabling Cameras on Avatars to the Safety System.\n\nI know right now you need to friend people in order to see their cameras, but this would be much easier, since you wouldn't need to friend everyone you want to show a animation with a camera or so.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Addition to the Safety System",
      "parentID": "5baf322ce038c00e28fd174a",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5ba479515716a9780fd56369",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: As the system currently stands, yes. If cameras were not restricted to friends however, it could easily be part of the safety system for the same reason.\n\nA lot of things can be done with cameras, and as is it's only \"trusted\" people (friends) who can see them. If in the safety system, lower end would be automatically blocked keeping performance up from those who abuse it, but allow higher ranks to make use of it.\n\nPeople could also override it for individuals with the \"show all\" (show avatar?)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
