      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Tupper bb. The safety system had to be implemented because of the pitfalls of the \"performance scope\" as it stands in VR. We wouldn't need individual toggles of a safety system if the point wasn't to observe increased performance/the ability to choose what we see or don't see. As a few others mentioned, nearly anything can be used to cause overloads/crashing, and cameras on avatars is certainly no exception.",
